applesmc: get the SMC from the LED with container_of, not drvdata

On top of t2linux patch 3001. applesmc_brightness_set() took
dev_get_drvdata(led_cdev->dev), but led_cdev->dev is the LED class device,
whose drvdata is the led_classdev itself. Since the default "nand-disk"
trigger sets the brightness during led_classdev_register(), every pre-T2 Mac
with a keyboard-backlight key wrote through a bogus pointer and oopsed in
probe. The work function already uses container_of; do the same here.

--- a/drivers/hwmon/applesmc.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/applesmc.c
@@ -1467,7 +1467,7 @@
 static void applesmc_brightness_set(struct led_classdev *led_cdev,
 						enum led_brightness value)
 {
-	struct applesmc_device *smc = dev_get_drvdata(led_cdev->dev);
+	struct applesmc_device *smc = container_of(led_cdev, struct applesmc_device, backlight_dev);
 	int ret;
 
 	smc->backlight_state[0] = value;
